I've got the best character I've had in nh3.1... an archaeologist, 300 hp, 
AC -30, all the intrinsics, the whole bit.  I found a temple and got lots
of golden glows and protection (I killed the gnome town, I admit it) from
the gods... blessed +4 rustproof Snickersnee, gray dragon scale, amulet of
reflection, helm of telepathy, everything a young demigod in training could
hope for!

Okay... I went down to level 20 (where my temple is) and wasted seven wands
of create monster having fun with the altar, then went to go to level 21: as
soon as I stepped downstairs, seg fault.  No map even appeared... so I had
the system guys restore my file and I tried it from the other direction
(level tport to 22 w/ cursed scroll and came up the stairs)... seg fault. 
I had several cursed scrolls, so right now I've gone down, beat the medusa
and the castle, and tport'ed back up to polypile at my temple... I know I
can win with this guy, no problem, but how?  I can't tport once I have the
amulet, and I'll seg fault when I come up with the amulet and hit level 21!!!

Okay, so far I (and a friend on the system staff) have tried two things.
First, we copied Foo22.Z into Foo21.Z... no dice, it said the level was out
of order and put me in the score file as "a trickery".  Hmmph.  Next we tried
deleting Foo21.Z in the hopes that it'd generate a new one... it says "can't
find file... someone deleted it" and put me down as "a trickery" again!  I'm
really not trying to cheat here, I'd just like a level 21 to exist!!!

So... please (via email, I can't keep up here) give me some suggestions...
either some way to edit the save file so it doesn't think I've ever been to 21
(and generates a new one) or something... anything, please!!!  I'd hate to
write this guy off without a fight...

Thanks much,
Hank.
